# Required build variables for Cod.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values BEFORE building:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# These are consumed by build.sh / release.sh and injected via --dart-define.
#
# SECURITY NOTES
# --------------
# • GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET is a *confidential* OAuth credential. It gets
#   compiled into the app binary, so it is effectively PUBLIC once you
#   distribute the app. For a real deployment:
#     - Prefer switching to PKCE with a public "client_id" (no secret),
#       or route token exchange through a backend.
#     - If you must ship a desktop/mobile client, register it as a
#       "Desktop"/"TV and Limited Input" OAuth client so Google knows it
#       is an installed app, and treat the secret as non-confidential.
#     - Immediately rotate (revoke + regenerate) any secret that has
#       ever been exposed in a build artifact, commit, or log.
#
# • SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is not secret by design, BUT the app uses it to
#   read/write the `tasks` table directly. This is only safe if your
#   Supabase project has ROW LEVEL SECURITY enabled with per-user
#   policies. If RLS is off, anyone with this (public) key can read and
#   delete every user's tasks. Harden RLS before shipping.
#
# • Never commit the real `.env` file. Only .env.example (this file)
#   is allowed in version control.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-client-secret
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your_anon_key
